WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.858
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 3: Food and Health.

2
00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:08.401
Good food is one of the best gifts a family shares each day.

3
00:00:08.481 --> 00:00:13.248
In this unit you learn to talk
about food and health in English.

4
00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:22.259
You read about where food comes from, how to keep it clean
and safe, and why fresh food helps your body and your brain.

5
00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:29.150
You give clear instructions, ask good questions,
and compare healthy and unhealthy choices.

6
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:35.814
Along the way you meet twenty new words, from
sandwich and rice to pesticide and famine,

7
00:00:35.894 --> 00:00:40.736
and you use grammar that explains
rules, reasons and comparisons.

8
00:00:40.816 --> 00:00:45.659
By the end you are ready for this
unit's story, The Bitter Lunch,

9
00:00:45.739 --> 00:00:50.429
about a girl named Amal who
learns to check her food with care.

10
00:00:50.509 --> 00:00:56.790
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:05.504
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
describe many foods, and talk about where food comes from.

12
00:01:05.584 --> 00:01:11.807
You will also explain why fresh, clean
food is good for your body and your brain.

13
00:01:11.887 --> 00:01:17.642
You will also give clear instructions
using imperatives (“Wash the fruit.”)

14
00:01:17.722 --> 00:01:20.521
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:26.303
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
sandwich, lamb, rice, spice, bakery, fresh.

16
00:01:26.383 --> 00:01:31.566
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

17
00:01:31.646 --> 00:01:35.659
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

18
00:01:35.739 --> 00:01:40.432
The reading sequence includes From
Farm to Plate and A Poster on the Wall.

19
00:01:40.512 --> 00:01:41.335
Read actively.

20
00:01:41.415 --> 00:01:45.786
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

21
00:01:45.866 --> 00:01:49.979
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

22
00:01:50.059 --> 00:01:53.908
The first language focus is Modal Verbs — must and might.

23
00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:58.735
Modal verbs are special helping
verbs, and this unit uses two of them.

24
00:01:58.815 --> 00:02:03.561
Must shows that something is necessary
or very important, like a rule.

25
00:02:03.641 --> 00:02:07.421
Might shows that something is possible, but not certain.

26
00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:14.936
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:15.016 --> 00:02:18.917
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: My Favourite Meal.

28
00:02:18.997 --> 00:02:23.288
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:23.368 --> 00:02:26.616
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:26.696 --> 00:02:30.074
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:30.154 --> 00:02:31.704
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:38.717
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:38.797 --> 00:02:42.117
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:42.197 --> 00:02:50.122
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
